  "solution": "Given:\n\nThe successive discounts are 5%, 10% and p%\n\nSingle discount = 31.6%\n\nConcept: If there are three successive discounts of a%, b% and c% on MP\n\nSP = MP(100 - a)/100 × (100 - b)/100 × (100 - c)/100 \n\nFormula used:\n\nSP = MP × (100 - D%)/100\n\nD% = (D/MP) × 100\n\nCalculation:\n\nLet MP be x\n\nSP = x × (100 - 5)/100 × (100 - 10)/100 × (100 - p)/100\n\n⇒ SP = x × 95/100 × 90/100 × (100 - p)/100\n\n⇒ x × 95/100 × 90/100 × (100 - p)/100 = x × (100 - 31.6)/100 \n\n⇒ x × 19/20 × 9/10 × (100 - p)/100 = x × 68.4/100 \n\n⇒ (100 - p)/100 = 2 × 68.4/171\n\n⇒ (100 - p)/100 = 0.8\n\n⇒ (100 - p) = 80\n\n⇒ p = 20\n\nThe value of P is 20%.",
